r10rggen6 purpose-built goldens (Rggen pass 6).  Each file isolates ONE law
decoded this pass; run with

  bash tools/probe/r10rggen6golden.sh <dir> <file.sv>     # Surelog golden
  bash /tmp/r10rggen6_g/mine.sh <file.sv> pa|tr|uu        # ours + census

t1  § elabParamTsRebind      def-view param ts rebind reaches every ELAB
                             instance BUT THE FIRST (u0 bit, u1/u2 logic).
t2  § elabParamTsRebind      "first" is DEPTH-FIRST instance order
                             (top.m0.s0 keeps `bit`, top.u0 / gb[*] do not).
t3  § elabOvRefIntConst      an override actual that is a bare ref to a
                             parameter copies THAT parameter's fold encoding
                             (WORDS=DATA_WIDTH/BUS_WIDTH -> INT; literal and
                             port-param actuals -> UINT).
t4  § genLpTsFoldBounds      a GEN-SCOPE localparam's packed-range bounds are
                             folded; a module-level parameter's are not.
t5  § cast-seal              a mul/div/pow inside an explicit SIZE CAST does
                             not make a gen-lp fold signed (A/K vs C/D/E/F/H)
                             + § genLpCaSharedBareTs first sighting (J).
t6  = u2r ParameterInGenScopeInitializedWithLongConstant (CA-read localparam,
                             value-only logic clone).
t7  § genLpCaSharedBareTs    a `bit [3:0]` localparam READ by a cont_assign
                             still binds a LOGIC value-only clone.
t8  § genLpCaSharedBareTs    the discriminator, two sibling localparams of
                             identical type: the one passed as an
                             instantiation override keeps its own declaration
                             typespec, the one read by an assign gets the
                             bare logic clone.
t9  § retUnbasedSizing       `return '1` sizes to the RETURN TYPE and loses
                             the quote (BIN:1111 sz 4 / BIN:1 sz 1), while a
                             written `assign o = '0` keeps it.
